{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788193594,"nonce":"/xjqJHlmbbc86RtIwGtNACEBAD0=","message":"HANDOVER — orchestrator session 7 (dorian's Linux box), 2026-08-31.\nWork moves to BORGES, which can run the bench and has the decompiled tree.\nEverything pushed: main `9793d0d`, four spec branches, all bug refs.\n\n**17 of 25 done** (1.8 and 3.4 closed earlier this session; seek-at-will shipped\nand closed but was filed after the original 25). RUNLOG's session-7 sections\nhave the full account.\n\nREAD FIRST, BEFORE DISPATCHING ANYTHING: `2f2796e`\n\n**Verify the issue backlog before building to it.** 14 issues were filed today,\nmost from PLAYING rather than reading specs — which is a good source of issues\nand a bad source of CAUSES. Two of my filed diagnoses were wrong:\n\n- `1eb2262` — I blamed a pawn spawn for reordering the roster. Wrong. The real\n  cause is the attention score moving with mood. **A fix built to the issue as\n  written would have left the bug in place.**\n- `cc8988c` — I argued \"the fight is over\" needed judgement by conflating\n  `dangerWatcher.DangerRating` with `threats.hostiles`. They disagreed by 3 live.\n\nBoth corrected on their issues. The pattern is the risk, not those two. Every\nissue a worker INVESTIGATED rather than implemented came back better than its\nspec. `2f2796e` systematises that as a verification pass.\n\nFOUR BRANCHES, BUILT 0/0, NONE VERIFIED, NONE MERGED\n\n| branch | issue | note |\n|---|---|---|\n| `spec/orders-makingfor` | `32b9e01` | **acceptance BEFORE audit** — see below |\n| `spec/auto-arm-lever` | `1a072fa` | already merged with main, clean |\n| `spec/stable-pawn-order` | `1eb2262` | corrected my diagnosis |\n| `spec/manual-work-priorities` | `e8f2c32` | unblocks 8 of 3.4's checks |\n\nOnly `DESIGN.md` overlaps between them — three additive decisions-log entries,\nkeep all. `manual-work-priorities` and `stable-pawn-order` also both edit\n`accept/3.4-pawn-orders.{md,py,ps1}`; the `.py`/`.ps1` auto-merge, the `.md`\nconflicts additively. **That collision was my dispatch error** — two workers at\noverlapping files, which ORCHESTRATION-PROMPT explicitly warns against. Nothing\nlost; each had its own worktree.\n\n**`orders-makingfor` wants acceptance first, not audit first.** Its whole claim\nis a RUNTIME side effect (calling `orders` writes a 500-600 tick colony-wide\ncooldown onto a bill). An audit can only re-read the source the worker already\nread. Worse, the instrument needed to MEASURE it landed in the same branch as\nthe fix, so the \"before\" reading cannot be taken against main at all. Use phase\nM in `accept/32b9e01-orders-makingfor.md` — it needs no instrumentation: on main\n`orders` returns NO entry for an ingredient-starved bill; on the branch it\nreturns a `blocked` entry with the game's own MissingMaterials string. The\nfixture table names four ways to get a green run for the wrong reason.\n\nTHE DESIGN DECISION THAT CAME OUT OF TODAY, now in DESIGN.md\n\n**Deterministic goes in the mod; the playbook carries judgement. Judgement is\nCHOOSING a policy, not executing one.** Evan: \"what can be in the mod should be.\"\nThe test is whether every branch is computable from state the observers already\npublish — if not, name the missing read rather than reaching for the playbook.\nWhat feels like judgement at execution time usually means a policy has not been\ndecided yet. This settles the same question for `cc8988c` (post-raid procedure)\nand for the attribution work.\n\nNEW HAZARD CLASSES FOUND, all in shipped code\n\n- **PawnSafe Class G** (`32b9e01`): the hazard is not always a getter. `orders`\n  cited its widget, copied the provider clause-for-clause, called no banned\n  accessor, and still mutated — because what it omitted lived in the provider's\n  CALLER.\n- **`Pawn_PlayerSettings.displayOrder` is Class A** (`1eb2262`): the field the\n  colonist bar draws by is assigned LAZILY BY THE UI into a scribed field. It is\n  the obvious thing to reach for to get \"the order the player sees\".\n- **A widget's citation-worthy content can be its EFFECT, not its gate**\n  (`e8f2c32`): the manual-priorities checkbox has no precondition at all, but it\n  fans `Notify_UseWorkPrioritiesChanged` to every pawn, and a bare field write\n  leaves the flip INERT.\n\nBENCH: `autostart.rws` intact at tick 89426 — 4 colonists, marine armour, needs\ntopped, Doctor and Hauling checked for all, 144-cell stockpile clear of the\npawns. NOT overwritten with the post-raid wreck. `Prefs.xml` is at 2560x1600\nfullscreen for watching; backup at `Prefs.xml.bak-640x480`, restore for\nunwatched runs. Zero red errors in every session today.\n\nRECOMMENDED ORDER: `2f2796e` (verify the backlog) -\u003e acceptance on\n`orders-makingfor` -\u003e audit+merge the other three -\u003e `1.9` (p1, blocks 3.3) -\u003e\n`3.5` (M1-critical) -\u003e `3.6`.","files":null}]}